# Architecture

## Interaction Engines (data-driven only)
Build reusable engines fed by JSON schemas — never hardcode curriculum inside UI logic:
1. Multiple Choice
2. Drag & Drop
3. Sentence Scramble
4. Cloze / Fill-in-the-Blanks
5. Error Correction

## Separation of Concerns
- Curriculum lives in isolated JSON content files.
- Components only render from typed schema props.
- Keep content loaders/adapters separate from presentational UI.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — content inside the component
const options = ["apple", "book", "cat"];

// ✅ GOOD — schema-driven
type MultipleChoiceItem = {
  id: string;
  prompt: string;
  options: string[];
  correctId: string;
};
function MultipleChoice({ item }: { item: MultipleChoiceItem }) { /* render only */ }
```

## Accessibility
- Mobile-first tap targets ≥ 48px.
- Robust RTL/LTR switching per content language.
- Audio feedback hooks structured for Web Audio / Tone.js (do not block UI on sound).
